- @noindex = true
.page__head
  %div
    %span.eyebrow Design
    %h1.page__title Logo variants
    %p.page__lede
      The wordmark without its tagline is the default now. Four Glif variations keep its letterforms and
      change only the surface. Pick one and the masthead uses it in this browser until you reset.
  %button.button.button--quiet{ type: 'button', data: { logo: '' } } Reset to the original

- variants = [['clean', '/images/logo/clean.png', 'The original artwork with the tagline cut off. The masthead default.'],
              ['original', '/images/000000book-logo-beta.png', 'As shipped, with the tagline.'],
              ['spray', '/images/logo/spray.jpg', 'Glif: the same letters with a spray halo and overspray.'],
              ['drips', '/images/logo/drips.jpg', 'Glif: the same letters with a few drips off the heavy strokes.'],
              ['chrome', '/images/logo/chrome.jpg', 'Glif: the same letters with a silver chrome fill.'],
              ['ghost', '/images/logo/ghost.jpg', 'Glif: the same letters over a misregistered grey copy.'],
              ['fat-marker', '/images/logo/fat-marker.jpg', 'Glif, first round: marker weight with drips, letterforms redrawn.']]
.logos
  - variants.each do |name, src, note|
    .logos__variant{ data: { logo_variant: name } }
      .logos__masthead
        = image_tag src, alt: "#000000book.com wordmark, #{name} variant", class: 'logos__image'
      .logos__meta
        %span.meta= name
        %span.logos__note= note
        %button.button{ type: 'button', data: { logo: src } } Use in masthead
